{"id":"n5-120","title":"なんで～ (nande～)","jlptLevel":5,"shortExplanation":"Asking the reason or cause; 'why', 'how come'.","longExplanation":"The なんで grammar point is used to ask the reason or cause behind something. It can be translated as 'why' or 'how come' in English. It is a casual way of asking for an explanation, and it can be used with verbs, い-adjectives, な-adjectives, and nouns.","formation":"なんで + [phrase or sentence]","examples":[{"jp":"なんで遅れたの？","romaji":"Nande okureta no?","en":"Why were you late?","words":[{"surface":"なんで","vocabId":"1611020","reading":"なんで"},{"surface":"遅れ","vocabId":"1422020","reading":"おくれ","baseForm":"遅れる"},{"surface":"た","vocabId":null},{"surface":"の","vocabId":null},{"surface":"？","vocabId":null}],"patternWordIndices":[0]},{"jp":"なんでこの部屋はこんなに汚いの？","romaji":"Nande kono heya wa konna ni kitanai no?","en":"Why is this room so dirty?","words":[{"surface":"なんで","vocabId":"1611020","reading":"なんで"},{"surface":"この","vocabId":null},{"surface":"部屋","vocabId":"1499320","reading":"へや"},{"surface":"は","vocabId":null},{"surface":"こんなに","vocabId":null},{"surface":"汚い","vocabId":"1178940","reading":"きたない"},{"surface":"の","vocabId":null},{"surface":"？","vocabId":null}],"patternWordIndices":[0]},{"jp":"なんで彼女は怒っているの？","romaji":"Nande kanojo wa okotte iru no?","en":"Why is she angry?","words":[{"surface":"なんで","vocabId":"1611020","reading":"なんで"},{"surface":"彼女","vocabId":"1483150","reading":"かのじょ"},{"surface":"は","vocabId":null},{"surface":"怒っ","vocabId":"1445690","reading":"おこる","baseForm":"怒る"},{"surface":"て","vocabId":null},{"surface":"いる","vocabId":"1577980","reading":"いる"},{"surface":"の","vocabId":null},{"surface":"？","vocabId":null}],"patternWordIndices":[0]},{"jp":"なんで今日は休みなの？","romaji":"Nande kyou wa yasumi na no?","en":"Why is today a holiday?","words":[{"surface":"なんで","vocabId":"1611020","reading":"なんで"},{"surface":"今日","vocabId":"1579110","reading":"きょう"},{"surface":"は","vocabId":null},{"surface":"休み","vocabId":"1227500","reading":"やすみ"